Clippy pedantic flags this as 'the following explicit lifetimes could be elided: a'. The 'a lifetime on the impl block is redundant because the function signature and struct definition already relate the lifetime through the &[u8] parameter:

  impl NormalizedIter<'_> {
      fn new(bytes: &[u8]) -> Self {

This is not a correctness issue, but explicit lifetimes that Rust can elide add noise.
